Subject: Fail the load cleanly when an allocation fails

The loader's heaps, hash map and document are allocated with unchecked
malloc() and calloc(), so running out of memory while loading a large
document dereferences NULL instead of returning NULL.

Check each allocation the loader makes. A failure inside
parse_attributes() (an attribute or an id entry) sets document->failed,
which the loop tests after each start tag; every failure leaves through
the existing error path, so plutosvg_document_load_from_data() returns
NULL and has called destroy_func(closure), as for a parse error. A failed
hash-map resize keeps the old buckets.

plutovg's own growth arrays are not covered: plutovg_array_ensure() has no
failure path, and changing it touches every caller.

zusvg: .agents/design.md §9, §17 D4. Offered upstream.

